Sender brands and optional local artwork
=======================================

Mail Code Filler is licensed under the MIT License; see LICENSE.

Brand names and trademarks belong to their respective owners. No third-party
brand artwork is distributed in this repository or its public releases. The
default app uses brand-colored initial monograms when local artwork is absent.
Brand identification does not imply authentication, sponsorship, affiliation,
or endorsement.

Sources/Core/Resources/sender-brands.json records sender domains, colors, and
official source metadata for optional personal builds: Apple App Store artwork
URLs and first-party website icon URLs, with source dimensions and review notes.
scripts/fetch-sender-icons.py can generate local, Git-ignored Sender imagesets
from those recorded sources. It does not change the source catalog. Follow the
README local-build instructions and the relevant owners' terms; do not include
these locally generated images in public releases.

The catalog's `license: "none"` means that no per-image SPDX license identifier
was supplied. It does not grant reproduction rights or put an image in the
public domain. The project's MIT License grants no rights to third-party
trademarks or artwork. `publicReleaseReviewed: false` and any seasonal-artwork
warnings remain source-review metadata, not permission to redistribute images.
